1. She once mistook "Google" for "goggles" when first using the internet as a child. (Verbatim: "i thought they said google so i went on to like google google.com or something like that or and i just remember looking at this website with like goggles and i was like what the heck am i supposed to do here")

2. Her first internet experience involved her parents letting her use the computer alone, leading to her downloading viruses and junk. (Verbatim: "they left me to to my own devices because that's what you do... fast forward a bit i've absolutely overloaded the computer we have computer viruses and downloaded absolute utter crap")

3. She searched for games to play online during her early internet use, which later inspired her to put Pokémon cards inside her PC. (Verbatim: "i looked for games to play... then led to my future self or was it yeah putting pokemon cards inside the pc hoping to")

4. She has a recurring joke or interest in the toy "Bop It" and has considered doing a stream playing it. (Verbatim: "i still wanna get a bop it one day... one day i'll get to play bop it and not just make jokes about it")

5. She once overslept because she was stuck in a dream where she was waiting for a McDonald's delivery that never arrived. (Verbatim: "i didn't wake up from my dream was because in my dream I'd ordered McDonald's and I was waiting for it to arrive and it didn't and I guess I couldn't wake up until my order arrived in my dream")

6. In the same dream, she ordered McDonald's twice, and the first order was unsatisfactory—a salad mixed with a few fries. (Verbatim: "I'd actually ordered McDonald's twice in this dream... they'd run out of fries and like gave me like some weird like salad mixed with a few leftover fries")

7. She associates the number 666 with bad luck, calling 40,000 minutes “a cursed number of minutes” and noting it equals 666 hours. (Verbatim: "that's a cursed number of minutes that's 666 um spooky spooky")

8. She recalls YouTube originally having a 10-minute video limit, which required content to be split into multiple parts. (Verbatim: "once upon a time... youtube videos were a maximum of like 10 minutes i want to say 10 minutes and if you wanted to watch anything you'd have like part one of three")

9. She finds it frustrating when YouTube causes streaming issues, personifying it as "YouTube-kun" being mean. (Verbatim: "Um, YouTube-kun, why must you be so mean? Why? Why? Why? Why?")

10. She has a nostalgic memory of early YouTube, including the absence of ads and the use of stars for ratings. (Verbatim: "once upon a time when youtube looked very very different when there were no adverts and things had stars") [end of text]



1. She had a dog that passed away after reaching old age and living a good life. (Verbatim: "dogs passed away um but it reached it reached old age like it did reach a very old age... it was a brilliant dog")

2. She was not allowed to walk the family dog because it was too hyper and she was considered too small to handle it. (Verbatim: "i wasn't actually allowed to walk that dog um um because it was too hyper... they thought i would get pulled away by the dog")

3. Her older brother was responsible for walking the family dog. (Verbatim: "only my my um my older brother was allowed to help with walking the dog")

4. The family dog had an extremely high jump, capable of reaching the top of her head when it jumped. (Verbatim: "the dog could always like reach the top of my head when it jumped it had such an insane jump")

5. As a child, she accompanied her brother on a walk with the dog, during which the dog scared a little girl by jumping over her multiple times in a field. (Verbatim: "the dog decides that it would be perfect to use her as like a um jumping thing... she jumped out of her skin like she was terrified")

6. She had to apologize to a child and her parents after the family dog frightened the child during a walk. (Verbatim: "i had to like apologize a lot um because the girl started crying... she was very upset um yeah so i had to apologize")

7. The family dog was very cheeky and would try to eat anything it found, including non-food items. (Verbatim: "it got to a point where um this dog was so cheeky that it would um try and like eat anything it found okay")

8. The dog wore a muzzle not because it was aggressive, but to prevent it from eating everything, which caused people to mistakenly fear it. (Verbatim: "owners might put a muzzle on the dog but not for biting... the muzzle's there because this dog can't control itself around food")

9. She believes people should not judge a dog by its muzzle, as it may not indicate aggression. (Verbatim: "don't judge don't judge a dog by its muzzle okay... it's not like it's it's like a code of shame")

10. The dog never harmed anyone and was completely harmless despite its intimidating appearance. (Verbatim: "never ever hurt a person ever") [end of text]



1. She values her "zatsu dance" and membership streams and does not want to give them up. (Verbatim: "i don't want to give up my zatsu dance and chatting with you all")

2. She streams frequently, averaging around 10 streams per week. (Verbatim: "i think with like on average 10 streams a week")

3. She wants to make people happy and help others who are similar to her. (Verbatim: "i want to make people happy i want to help any little ellie's out there")

4. She previously kept a physical diary but stopped because she tended to write too much. (Verbatim: "whenever i used to have an actual physical diary before i stopped writing those because they became my own")

