1. She does not know how to drive. (Verbatim: "i don't i don't drive so i if i finished like a long shift i'd have to get the bus back")
2. She has a strong dislike of long work shifts and finds them tiring. (Verbatim: "wait 48 hour shifts oh gosh oh gosh no oh i just want to relax with you all and i feel bad that you had to do these long shifts")
3. She used to work long shifts in a job before transitioning to remote work. (Verbatim: "i remember having long shifts and like the thing that would really um suck when i used to have to do long shifts anywhere")
4. She developed a lot of patience from waiting for unreliable buses in England. (Verbatim: "i think a lot of my patience actually developed from from waiting for buses i'll be honest like i'm pretty certain i gained a lot of my patience there")
5. Public transportation in England, especially buses, is often late, doesn't show up, or is too full to board. (Verbatim: "buses in england aren't very good at being on time um like they're not they don't turn up um most of the time they don't turn up")
6. She suffers from travel sickness and cannot read or look at her phone on moving vehicles. (Verbatim: "i get travel sick really easily so um if i was to read i can't read or really look at my phone very much when i'm on on a moving vehicle")
7. She requires a window seat on buses to avoid feeling sick. (Verbatim: "i'd always have to make sure i have a window seat as well like um for a bus if i couldn't see out the window i genuinely get really sick")
8. As a child, she often got sick on school bus trips and would vomit, which affected her social reputation. (Verbatim: "i used to always be that kid that would throw up um which definitely didn't help with the whole like you know already not popular")
9. She used to take up to two hours to commute to work via bus, despite it being only a 10–15 minute drive by car. (Verbatim: "it would take me it would take me two hours to get there or if i'm lucky like an hour and a half")
10. She previously worked as a developer and transitioned to working from home, which she is very grateful for. (Verbatim: "when this whole work from home thing came and i was still working as like a developer i was so thankful") [end of text]



1. She previously worked as a software developer before becoming a VTuber. (Verbatim: "whole work from home thing came and i was still working as like a developer i was so thankful")

2. She had a negative work experience with a previous employer who showed no concern when she was on a bus that caught on fire. (Verbatim: "my manager saying they really need me in and i'm like i'm not choosing to to be on the bus that's on in flames here like excuse me")

3. She used to commute long hours via public transport, often leaving at 7 AM for a 9 AM start to ensure punctuality. (Verbatim: "if i started at nine i would usually leave at seven even if it wasn't a two-hour journey... because then be mad if you're late")

4. She had to walk 30 minutes to an earlier bus stop to secure a seat due to overcrowding on buses near her workplace. (Verbatim: "i'd actually have to walk for like um usually about 30 minutes... just so i could get a seat on the bus")

5. She experienced a bus catching fire while she was riding it, specifically at the back where she was seated. (Verbatim: "the bus caught on fire okay like full flames... it was the back of the bus that set up on fire")

6. She felt guilt over being late to work due to unreliable public transportation despite her strong work ethic. (Verbatim: "i would just feel so guilty when when i was late because i genuinely would be trying but sometimes the bus just doesn't turn up")

7. She was once written up at jobs for being late, which was outside her control due to transit issues. (Verbatim: "i've actually been like written up because i've been late and things you know")

8. Her difficult past work experiences were a key motivation for becoming a VTuber. (Verbatim: "if my previous jobs didn't suck so much... i wouldn't be here with you guys right now")

9. During secondary school, she fraudulently used an expired male student's bus pass to ride for free. (Verbatim: "someone gave me their old bus pass... i did get caught like once or twice one for it being expired")

10. She ran away from transit authorities when caught using a fake bus pass during her school years. (Verbatim: "they were like i'm gonna have to confiscate that and i was like... and then i ran i was like good luck chasing me punk") [end of text]



1. She has experience working at a zoo and looked after pigs and monkeys. (Verbatim: "I looked after pigs when I was at the zoo... I used to look after little monkeys...")
